  year={2019},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={23-39},
  abstract={The main steps of electric distribution system planning can be depicted by the flow chart. The flow chart starts with identifying the system capacity to enable the planner to model the network loading and performance and identify system inadequacies and constraints. The planning process depends mainly on the factors such as demand forecast, planning policy, condition monitoring (CM), and reliability standards. This chapter summarizes the planning objectives of the distribution system. Distribution losses are inevitable consequences of distributing energy between the zone substations and consumers. Losses in distribution networks can be broken down into technical losses and non&#x2010;technical losses. The planners should think about the available solutions that can be applied to modify the distribution network installations to meet the load growth in the next 3 to 5 years. The solutions can be classified into two types: network solutions and nonnetwork solutions.},
  keywords={Planning;Maintenance engineering;Standards;Reliability;Monitoring;Asset management;Investment},
  doi={10.1002/9781119509332.ch3},
